==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*tīra-}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*dei-}}.

Cognate with Old Norse {{m|non|tírr||glory, renown}}. A variant of {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*tērīn-}}, gave Old High German {{m|goh|zierī}} (German {{m|de|Zier||splendour, beauty}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tiːr/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=tīr|m}}

# [[fame]]; [[glory]]; [[honour]]

